cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Claimstone: topics in, verdicts out"
abstract: >-
  Claimstone takes a set of topics and a frozen list of numbered questions, finds and
  legally obtains the readable literature on those topics, extracts what each source
  claims with every claim bound to a verbatim quote verified as an exact substring of the
  source, weighs the claims per question, and returns a verdict with its coverage. It
  reports "unanswered in the literature" and "never asked" as distinct states, and refuses
  to produce verdicts for a round that could not obtain enough of what it found.
message: "If you use this software, please cite it."
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Jonbj/claimstone"
authors:
  - given-names: Stefano
    family-names: Del Gobbo
keywords:
  - evidence synthesis
  - systematic review
  - meta-analysis
  - provenance
  - citation verification
  - reproducible research
